sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign 2026-11-04, topology templates plan points 3 and 4 (ADR 0247). Open: a complete stock-to-app-dev run (the 2026-11-04 attempt stopped at a 404 after 5 min 27 s).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · nightly
  %% kind: template.build
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane V icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane I icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant V as Task VM<br/>nested topology
  participant I as Incus host<br/>holds templates
  Note over GW: Nightly build<br/>task group #812
  %%> When:
  %%> - once a night, for the running release
  %%> Why a task group:
  %%> - it gets a task VM, a workspace and Pi the normal way, and the morning result shows on the task board
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-template-build
  SW->>V: Provision the task VM<br/>task:start
  SW->>V: Build from stock Ubuntu<br/>nested Gateway · dev · prod
  %%> Why from stock:
  %%> - proves a new Node reaches the release from nothing, which the templates never do again
  SW->>V: Run every case<br/>test cases · all
  SW->>V: Compare with the templates<br/>doctor · fresh vs converged
  %%> Why:
  %%> - any difference is converge drift: the upgrade path and the fresh path ended in different states
  alt build passes
    SW->>I: Replace the templates<br/>fresh snapshots · publish image
    %%> Why:
    %%> - templates do not slowly drift away from a fresh install
  else a step fails
    SW->>V: Start Pi on the failure<br/>step · logs · diff
    %%> Pi decides by cause:
    %%> - an Orbit bug: fix it, prove it in the VM, open a PR
    %%> - an upstream break: pin the last working version and exclude it in `renovate.json`, PR with the reason
    %%> - infrastructure: rerun once, then report
    %%> Templates:
    %%> - the current templates stay
  end
  SW->>V: Destroy the task VM
  %%> When:
  %%> - always, after Pi ends
  SW-->>GW: Run ended
  Note over GW: Morning result<br/>passed · fix PR · report
